<http://example.org/kg/bolton_2006_cake_standard_blocking/bolton_2006_cake_standard_blocking_meta> a mkg:Metadata ;
    mkg:completeModel true ;
    mkg:description "The combined cake-standard blocking model describes fouling of a membrane by both cake formation on its surface and pore constriction within the membrane. It predicts filtered volume over time during constant-pressure operation and pressure over time during constant-flow operation, using Darcy’s law and the two mechanisms’ effects on filtration resistance. The model has two fitted parameters and is formulated with algebraic relations rather than dynamic state equations. The paper tested combined fouling models using human plasma IgG filtered through a sterilizing-grade PVDF membrane and BSA filtered through a virus-retention membrane, under both constant-pressure and constant-flow conditions. The cake-standard model improved fits in some tests, but the authors present it as most applicable when the observed fouling is consistent with both mechanisms, rather than as a model that fits a broad range of fouling curves." ;
    mkg:doi "10.1016/j.memsci.2004.12.053" ;
    mkg:form "algebraic" ;
    mkg:hasAssumption [ mkg:quote "The deposited aggregates were assumed to be permeable." ;
            mkg:reasoned false ;
            mkg:severity "warning" ;
            mkg:text "Deposited aggregates are permeable." ] ;
    mkg:hasFact [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Three experiments were performed using the 13 mm membrane holders. The permeate volume was measured as a function of time until the flux had declined 95% from its initial value of $ 1.13 \\times 10^{-3} $ m/s." ;
            mkg:text "Three constant-pressure IgG experiments used 13 mm holders and continued until flux had fallen by 95% from its initial value of 1.13 × 10⁻³ m/s." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The combined cake-standard and cake-intermediate models also provided good data fits and may be applicable to systems where these models are consistent with the experimentally observed fouling mechanisms." ;
            mkg:text "The cake-standard model is presented as a candidate for interpreting filtration data when the combined mechanisms match observed fouling, rather than as the paper’s general-purpose model for membrane sizing." ;
            mkg:topic "use" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Model: Cake-standard (Eq. (23)) | Model fit error, SSR: $ 6.27 \\times 10^{3} $" ;
            mkg:text "For constant-pressure BSA, the cake-standard model had an SSR of 6.27 × 10³, better than the four standalone fouling models but worse than the cake-complete and cake-intermediate models." ;
            mkg:topic "performance" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The BSA solution was filtered at a constant pressure through five samples of Viresolve 180 membrane in the 47 mm membrane holders. The permeate volume was measured as a function of time until the flux had declined 98% from its initial value of $ 3.58 \\times 10^{-4} $ m/s." ;
            mkg:text "Five constant-pressure BSA experiments used 47 mm holders and continued until flux had fallen by 98% from its initial value of 3.58 × 10⁻⁴ m/s." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The models derived in this study are less physically detailed than the model of Ho and Zydney and will therefore be less useful for estimation of physical parameters." ;
            mkg:text "The authors compare their combined models with Ho and Zydney 2000, describing their own models as less physically detailed but numerically simpler." ;
            mkg:topic "prior work" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Human plasma IgG (Seracare, Oceanside, CA) was prepared in pH 7.2 PBS at a concentration of 10.0 mg/mL." ;
            mkg:text "The human plasma IgG feed was prepared at 10.0 mg/mL in pH 7.2 PBS." ;
            mkg:topic "feed" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The model used three fitted parameters and an approximate solution was provided that allowed calculation of flux as a function of time without integrating." ;
            mkg:text "The earlier Ho and Zydney model used three fitted parameters and numerical integration for pressure-time or volume-time predictions." ;
            mkg:topic "prior work" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Bovine serum albumin (BSA, Sigma, St. Louis, MO) was prepared at 2.5 mg/mL concentration in pH 7.2 PBS buffer" ;
            mkg:text "The BSA feed was prepared at 2.5 mg/mL in pH 7.2 PBS." ;
            mkg:topic "feed" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "In this case the parameters used in the combined cake-standard model can be considered average values over the course of the run." ;
            mkg:text "The authors note that if the mechanisms become coupled during filtration, fitted parameters can represent average behavior over the run." ;
            mkg:topic "assumptions" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The paper evaluates fits against the reported filtration experiments but does not describe an independent validation dataset for the cake-standard model." ;
            mkg:topic "validation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Explicit equations were derived from Darcy's law that related pressure to time during constant flow operation, and volume to time during constant pressure operation." ;
            mkg:text "For constant-pressure operation, the cake-standard model calculates filtered volume as a function of time, while for constant-flow operation it calculates pressure as a function of time." ;
            mkg:topic "formulation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Data was collected every second for 1 h." ;
            mkg:text "Data were collected every second for one hour in the described constant-pressure setup." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "In this study only the parameter $ K_{s} $ was fit to the data." ;
            mkg:text "For the constant-pressure IgG comparison, the authors fit only the standard-blocking parameter in the standalone standard model rather than refitting the initial flux." ;
            mkg:topic "fitting" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "In this case the available membrane area will not decline over the course of the run." ;
            mkg:text "In the cake-standard model, the available membrane area remains constant over the run." ;
            mkg:topic "mechanisms" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The combined cake-standard model assumes that the two fouling mechanisms are independent and will occur throughout the run." ;
            mkg:text "The model treats cake formation and standard blocking as independent mechanisms that proceed throughout filtration." ;
            mkg:topic "assumptions" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "There are four mechanistic models that are typically used to describe fouling." ;
            mkg:text "The paper builds the combined model from established individual fouling laws associated with Grace 1956 and Hermia 1982." ;
            mkg:topic "prior work" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Eq. (22) reduces to the equation for cake filtration when $ K_{s} $ is small, and reduces to the equation for standard blocking when $ K_{c} $ is small." ;
            mkg:text "When one mechanism dominates, the cake-standard model reduces to the corresponding cake-filtration or standard-blocking model." ;
            mkg:topic "formulation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "They only provide improved fits of data that falls between the curves of their respective individual component models. They cannot fit data that resembles the complete blocking model predictions where the flux declines more slowly than other models initially, and more rapidly later in the run." ;
            mkg:text "The cake-standard model improves fits mainly for curves between the predictions of its two component models and cannot fit the described complete-blocking curve shape." ;
            mkg:topic "scope" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Durapore PVDF based membrane with a nominal pore size rating of 0.22 μm was run at 10 psi during constant pressure tests. Viresolve 180, a PVDF composite membrane composed of a thin ultraporous layer on top of a thicker microporous layer, was run at 30 psi during constant pressure tests of virus filtration membranes." ;
            mkg:text "Constant-pressure IgG tests used a transmembrane pressure of 10 psi, and constant-pressure BSA tests used 30 psi." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The resistance after fouling can be calculated by adding the resistance from standard blocking to the resistance from cake formation." ;
            mkg:text "The model combines cake filtration, in which a surface cake adds resistance, with standard blocking, in which material constricts pores from within." ;
            mkg:topic "mechanisms" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "An electronic balance aperture and a collection vessel were used to collect and measure the filtrate weight. The electronic balance consisted of a load cell (1042-3-I, Tedea Huntleigh, Covina, CA) that interfaced with a computer through a data acquisition board." ;
            mkg:text "The constant-pressure setup measured filtrate weight using a collection vessel and electronic balance with a load cell interfaced to a computer." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Viresolve 180, a PVDF composite membrane composed of a thin ultraporous layer on top of a thicker microporous layer" ;
            mkg:text "The BSA virus-filtration tests used Viresolve 180, a PVDF composite membrane with a thin ultraporous layer over a thicker microporous layer." ;
            mkg:topic "equipment" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Eq. (23) is applicable when $ \\alpha $ is not near 1 or -1. This will be the case when neither of the two fouling mechanisms dominates. When the parameter values indicate that one fouling mechanisms dominates the corresponding individual model should be used." ;
            mkg:text "The paper’s closed-form constant-pressure solution is stated to apply when its intermediate parameter is not near 1 or −1; when one mechanism dominates, the corresponding individual model should be used." ;
            mkg:topic "formulation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The data is the average of five runs and the error bars are one standard deviation." ;
            mkg:text "The BSA results were reported as the average of five runs, with error bars showing one standard deviation." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "During constant flow tests, a peristaltic pump (L/S Precision #WF77911-20, Cole Parmer, Vernon Hills, IL) with 16 gauge tubing (06409-16, Cole Parmer) was used to pump 10 mg/mL IgG through the Durapore membrane in the 47 mm holders at 579 L/m $ ^{2} $ h." ;
            mkg:text "Constant-flow IgG filtration was run at 579 L/m² h through Durapore membranes." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Standard blocking assumes that particles accumulate inside membranes on the walls of straight cylindrical pores." ;
            mkg:text "The standard-blocking mechanism represents particles accumulating on the walls of straight cylindrical pores." ;
            mkg:topic "mechanisms" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The paper does not report whether model code or the experimental data are publicly available." ;
            mkg:topic "availability" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Model: Cake-standard (Eq. (29)) | Model fit error, SSR: $ 1.35 \\times 10^{1} $" ;
            mkg:text "For constant-flow IgG, the cake-standard model had an SSR of 13.5, substantially below the standalone standard model’s SSR of 980." ;
            mkg:topic "performance" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The best fit of the data occurred with the combined cake-intermediate model, which had and SSR value slightly lower than the cake-complete model" ;
            mkg:text "For constant-flow IgG, the cake-standard model fit less well than the cake-intermediate and cake-complete models, whose SSR values were 0.58 and 1.36." ;
            mkg:topic "performance" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The cake-standard and cake-intermediate models were not as useful for fitting the predictions of the typical blocking models." ;
            mkg:text "The cake-standard model is less useful than the cake-complete model for fitting a broad range of individual-model predictions." ;
            mkg:topic "scope" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The best fit was determined by minimizing the sum of squared residuals (SSR) where the residual was equal to the difference between a data point and the model prediction." ;
            mkg:text "Model fits were assessed by minimizing the sum of squared residuals, with each residual defined as the difference between a measured point and its model prediction." ;
            mkg:topic "fitting" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Durapore PVDF based membrane with a nominal pore size rating of 0.22 μm was run at 10 psi during constant pressure tests." ;
            mkg:text "The IgG sterile-filtration tests used nominally 0.22 μm Durapore PVDF membranes in stainless-steel holders." ;
            mkg:topic "equipment" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "Three constant-flow IgG experiments measured pressure over time while the feed was pumped through 47 mm membrane holders." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The fits of the standard model alone were as good as the fits of the standard model combined with the complete blocking model, Eq. (18), the intermediate blocking model, Eq. (19), or the cake filtration model, Eq. (23)." ;
            mkg:text "For constant-pressure IgG, the standalone standard model fit about as well as the combined standard-and-cake model." ;
            mkg:topic "performance" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The combined cake-standard and cake-intermediate models also provided good data fits and may be applicable to systems where these models are consistent with the experimentally observed fouling mechanisms." ;
            mkg:text "The cake-standard model is most applicable when the observed fouling is consistent with both cake formation and standard blocking." ;
            mkg:topic "scope" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Five new fouling models that accounted for the combined effects of the different individual fouling mechanisms were derived from Darcy's law." ;
            mkg:text "The combined fouling models are derived from Darcy’s law." ;
